Intercom first desktop voice and context-mesh slice

Workstream ID: ic-06
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/5
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: One observable voice-to-existing-session-to-spoken-result loop
Dependencies: ic-02, ic-04, ic-05

Purpose:
  Implement the bounded desktop experience only after separate authorization
  and qualification. Tauri 2/Rust + React/TypeScript/Three.js is now the
  product candidate. The owner separately authorized an early fixture-only
  Electron UI, including transparent Floating Mesh, before the live prerequisites.
  Dependencies remain required for the real voice-to-existing-session loop.

Tasks:
  [x] Obtain authority and explicit Electron selection for the fixture prototype.
  [x] Build the isolated synthetic UI and real transparent Floating Mesh mode.
  [x] Add saved profile selection, request snapshots and bounded graph rendering.
  [x] Add explicit demo confirmation, ambiguity, cancellation and honest outcomes.
  [x] Verify native transparency/restoration, idle/minimized behavior and WebGL loss.
  [x] Add saved microphone choice, explicit brief checks and visible access/device errors.
  [x] Package and verify an unsigned Windows x64 portable EXE on disposable profiles.
  [ ] Publish the requested prototype prerelease and independently verify its assets.
  [ ] Finalize the product stack/dependencies from the live qualification receipts.
  [ ] Build an isolated desktop host, audio controls and selected speech pipeline.
  [ ] Constrain native commands and implement versioned bounded IPC contracts.
  [ ] Connect qualified inference/speech settings to the selectable profiles.
  [ ] Route finalized utterances with explicit context/session identity.
  [ ] Implement terminal handoff and approved background dispatch.
  [ ] Render a spherical mesh with observed activity and unknown-coverage states.
  [ ] Persist job outcomes and deliver accurate notifications/spoken summaries.
  [ ] Cover ambiguity, permission, failure, cancellation and accessible fallback.
  [ ] Document actual build/test/launch commands and remaining evidence limits.

Acceptance criteria:
  The docs/roadmap.md first-slice scenario passes on disposable test data.
  Voice remains available while a request runs without model-based status polling.
  No fabricated reads, false completion, unrestricted tools or duplicate dispatch.
  Playback interruption is separate from task cancellation.
  Proposed runtime isolation is demonstrated, not inferred from different paths.
  Human voice/visual acceptance is recorded separately from automated checks.
  Profile changes apply at a request boundary without changing running jobs,
  permissions or approved providers; default performance meets agreed budgets.
  Host authority, request/outbox transactions and snapshot resynchronization
  follow docs/runtime-contracts.md; browser mocks are not native-app evidence.

Completion evidence:
  Fixture sub-slice: Electron 45.2.1, React/TypeScript/Vite and Three.js; exact
  dependency lock, local build and launch commands in README/docs/prototype.md.
  npm run lint and npm run build pass; seven Vitest cases and six Playwright
  desktop scenarios pass. Actual Electron captures have alpha-zero corner
  pixels and visible mesh pixels; both workspace/floating screenshots inspected.
  Mode toggling, original bounds, hover/keyboard restoration, pinning, sandbox/
  context isolation, narrow preload actions, profile snapshots/persistence,
  explicit targets, terminal cancellation, honest completion, WebGL loss and
  idle/minimized frame scheduling are covered using disposable profiles.
  Native minimize/show events supplement browser visibility for rendering pause.
  Local system-voice output is optional/off by default; no listening assessment.
  Added exact-device selection/persistence, immediate track cleanup, camera
  denial, missing-device and access/enumeration failure checks using fake media.
  All six scenarios pass against the packaged executable. The portable EXE
  itself separately passes startup, ASAR UI, microphone check and floating
  restoration. Its inspected archive has seven runtime files; notices included,
  private stores/profiles/credentials/tests excluded. EXE is unsigned, x64 only.
  Prerelease publication is pending. No continuous microphone input, wake word,
  mesh import, Agency session, terminal dispatch, durable jobs, installer or
  human acceptance. Live criteria remain open.
  Known limits: lazy 3D chunk warning; moderate minimatch development-tool
  advisory; production-only dependency audit rate-limited. No clean audit claim.

